tradition-component: kung-fu-shido

Oathbound's three Shido are personal to the practitioner and separate from Gaoshou's five institutional Style Shido. One of Gaoshou's five Style Shido—the Duan Wei 1 Shido—is also the Kung Fu Domain's Core Shido. A Gaoshou school defines its five Style Shido, including this Core Shido. All eight count separately toward the normal Shido cap, and an eligible trait may carry every distinct applicable Shido as separate Required Disadvantage/Pact limitations, subject to the normal limitation cap and trait-specific exclusions.

Additional Style Compatibility: Before beginning instruction in a second or later Gaoshou Style, the practitioner must already possess, or be legally able and willing to accept, that Style's Core Shido and at least three of its five fixed Style Shido in total. The Core Shido counts toward the three. This is a compatibility test only: it grants no Shido early or for free, and all Shido are still gained at the Style's normal Duan Wei stages. A Shido is acceptable only if the character can legally carry it under Kung Fu's Domain rules and the applicable Shido cap, and it does not irreconcilably contradict another fixed self-imposed mental disadvantage. A practitioner who fails this test cannot begin instruction in that Style.
